      "name": null,
      "problem": "The projection of the intersection between the hyperbolic paraboloid $z=-9{x}^{2}+(y+3)^{2}$, and the plane $z=4$ onto the $xy$-plane is a hyperbola. Find the center of this hyperbola.",
      "worked_solution": "To find the intersection of the paraboloid and the plane $z=4$, we substitute $z=4$ into the equation of the paraboloid, and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-9{x}^{2}+(y+3)^{2} & =z \\\\ -9{x}^{2}+(y+3)^{2} & =4 \\\\ -\\frac{9{x}^{2}}{4}+\\frac{(y+3)^{2}}{4} & =1 \\\\ -\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4/9}+\\frac{(y+3)^{2}}{4} & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis gives us the equation of a hyperbola in the $xy$-plane that has its center at $(0,-3).$",
