      "dom_id": "question-73861",
      "name": null,
      "problem": "Given the hyperbolic paraboloid $(x-4)^{2}-\\frac{(y+1)^{2}}{7}=z-12$, find its intercepts with the $y$-axis.",
      "worked_solution": "To find the $y$-intercepts of the paraboloid, we substitute $x=0$ and $z=0$ in the equation of the paraboloid:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(0-4)^{2}-\\frac{(y+1)^{2}}{7} & =0-12 \\\\ 16-\\frac{(y+1)^{2}}{7} & =-12 \\\\ \\frac{(y+1)^{2}}{7} & =28 \\\\ (y+1)^{2} & =196 \\\\ y+1 & =\\pm 14 \\\\ y & =-1\\pm 14\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis gives the solutions $y=-15$ and $y=13.$\n\nTherefore, the intercepts with the $y$-axis are $(0,-15,0)$ and $(0,13,0).$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
