      "dom_id": "question-73864",
      "name": null,
      "problem": "Find the saddle point of the hyperbolic paraboloid $z+8={x}^{2}-(y+9)^{2}.$",
      "worked_solution": "The general equation of a hyperbolic paraboloid with a saddle point at $({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})$ is \n\n$$\nz-{z}_{0}=\\frac{(x-{x}_{0})^{2}}{{a}^{2}}-\\frac{(y-{y}_{0})^{2}}{{b}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nTo find the saddle point, we rewrite our equation as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z+8 & ={x}^{2}-(y+9)^{2} \\\\ z-(-8) & =\\frac{(x-0)^{2}}{1}-\\frac{(y-(-9))^{2}}{1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis gives us the equation of a hyperbolic paraboloid with a saddle point at $(0,-9,-8).$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
